WEBVTT

01:04.064 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:06.066 --> 01:09.736
DAECHI POLICE

01:20.455 --> 01:21.539
Are you a lord?

01:21.623 --> 01:22.832
Are you the judge?

01:22.916 --> 01:26.461
If you hit us, must we take it?
If you send us to Namsan, must we go?

01:26.544 --> 01:30.131
If you say I'm a thief, am I one?
If you send me to jail, must I go?

01:30.215 --> 01:32.967
The ring next to the porcelain jar.
The diamond ring.

01:34.344 --> 01:36.846
I've never even seen a diamond ring!

01:37.931 --> 01:39.057
It's not here.

01:39.891 --> 01:42.644
Who was that female officer?
Was it Yeon-sun?

01:42.727 --> 01:44.687
Tell her to come here
and search this girl.

01:44.771 --> 01:45.688
Yes, sir.

01:46.606 --> 01:49.609
Why would anyone need to search me?
I'm not a thief!

01:49.692 --> 01:51.820
See? You must really be hiding something.

01:52.862 --> 01:55.990
The lady's been turning a blind eye
to this girl taking money from a jar.

01:56.074 --> 01:58.785
-No, I earned that--
-How did you earn it?

01:59.744 --> 02:01.371
You're an illegal tutor, right?

02:02.914 --> 02:06.126
The lady let the girl handle bookkeeping
and overlooked her stealing

02:06.209 --> 02:07.919
because she was a working student.

02:09.295 --> 02:11.131
Do all poor people steal, then?

02:11.631 --> 02:14.425
Some people wouldn't steal
even if beaten into it.

02:14.509 --> 02:16.177
Let us search you, then.

02:16.261 --> 02:18.388
Why do I have to?

02:18.471 --> 02:20.598
I'm not a thief! Why should I have to…

02:20.682 --> 02:22.016
Something's off about you.

02:22.100 --> 02:25.145
What's your home phone number?
I need to see your father.

02:25.228 --> 02:28.940
Why do you need to see my father?
I'm not a thief!

02:29.023 --> 02:32.735
If you have nothing to hide, call him.
Acting like this is a sign of guilt!

02:32.819 --> 02:35.905
If I tell my father
I'm suspected of being a thief,

02:35.989 --> 02:38.158
it will tear his heart apart!

02:52.463 --> 02:55.258
-All buses to the dorms stop here--
-I get it. Leave.

02:56.009 --> 02:58.595
-I'm waiting for my bus home…
-Not heading to the base?

02:59.304 --> 03:02.265
-I'm on leave until Friday.
-Go back early, then.

03:02.348 --> 03:03.391
Sorry?

03:03.975 --> 03:05.852
Don't you dare date Geum-myeong. Got it?

03:08.605 --> 03:09.689
Why won't you answer?

03:16.571 --> 03:17.572
Are you two…

03:19.657 --> 03:20.742
dating?

03:22.410 --> 03:23.536
Are you testing me?

03:26.372 --> 03:29.000
-I got dumped.
-Dumped? You?

03:29.083 --> 03:30.543
I always get dumped.

03:34.589 --> 03:39.177
You're chasing girls instead of studying.
That's why you always get dumped.

03:39.260 --> 03:43.014
Did your dad tell you
to date around in college?

03:43.765 --> 03:44.807
It's not that.

03:45.975 --> 03:48.061
I was dumped eight times by Geum-myeong.

03:55.235 --> 03:57.362
Do you want one or something?

03:57.445 --> 03:59.697
It's okay. You should have it, Father.

04:03.159 --> 04:04.160
Well, Mr. Yang.

04:05.370 --> 04:06.621
Have a safe trip back.

04:07.497 --> 04:08.331
But why?

04:10.083 --> 04:11.251
Why doesn't she like you?

04:16.130 --> 04:16.965
I just think--

04:17.048 --> 04:19.801
It's because you're too…
You're too… You know?

04:20.843 --> 04:23.221
-You're dead meat.
-It's not that--

04:23.304 --> 04:25.932
She grew up watching me,
so her standards are high.

04:26.015 --> 04:29.560
Up until she turned five,
she said she'd marry me when she grew up.

04:29.644 --> 04:31.312
That's why you don't cut it.

04:31.396 --> 04:33.022
So just move on with your life.

04:33.106 --> 04:34.357
There's a lid for every pot.

04:35.400 --> 04:37.568
The reason we're on and off is--

04:37.652 --> 04:39.404
What does "on and off" even mean?

04:39.946 --> 04:41.281
-Well…
-What?

04:43.992 --> 04:47.161
She says I'm as quiet as a mouse
and that I'm not saying anything…

04:50.331 --> 04:53.418
You're as quiet as a mouse.
Why aren't you saying anything?

04:53.501 --> 04:54.419
To be ready.

04:54.502 --> 04:57.338
-You have the ring on, so that's it.
-Ready, go.

05:06.055 --> 05:06.889
Well,

05:08.057 --> 05:09.976
since you offered…

05:13.813 --> 05:14.647
No.

05:17.483 --> 05:18.318
Go away.

05:33.082 --> 05:34.375
You lied about the ring?

05:37.045 --> 05:38.338
She didn't take it, did she?

05:44.677 --> 05:46.554
Goodness gracious.

05:46.637 --> 05:50.433
Why send her to the police?
You usually just frame them and fire them.

05:51.893 --> 05:53.561
Who would believe a thief?

05:53.644 --> 05:55.271
We need to make it seem like

05:55.355 --> 05:58.649
she's spewing nonsense
because she's accused of being a thief

05:58.733 --> 06:00.318
to avoid any trouble later.

06:01.027 --> 06:02.445
If she starts a rumor

06:02.528 --> 06:06.032
that Oh Jenny from Daechi-dong
is looking for someone to take her exam,

06:06.115 --> 06:07.825
you and I will be in deep shit.

06:08.534 --> 06:11.454
My ring was stolen,
and that girl is the thief.

06:17.168 --> 06:19.629
I always tell you, don't I?

06:19.712 --> 06:22.215
Life is all about betting big
or going bust.

06:22.840 --> 06:25.760
Whether I'll crush or be crushed,

06:25.843 --> 06:28.096
that's a split-second decision.

06:28.805 --> 06:32.517
There's no need to pity those
whose wells have run dry.

06:33.184 --> 06:36.687
Don't be swayed by petty sentiments.
You need to be cold.

06:37.271 --> 06:39.148
That's how I made my money.

06:40.942 --> 06:44.737
So keep making good money.
You'll be in for it if your well runs dry.

06:45.738 --> 06:46.572
What?

06:47.323 --> 06:48.324
I take after you.

06:51.119 --> 06:56.082
You're saying
she stole the flower-shaped ring

06:56.874 --> 06:58.626
that's always here, right?

06:59.293 --> 07:00.128
Yeah.

07:01.129 --> 07:02.338
How dare she.

07:03.923 --> 07:06.092
-It's a diamond.
-Yes. Diamond.

07:07.677 --> 07:09.178
How many carats was it?

07:10.221 --> 07:11.389
About half a carat?

07:12.515 --> 07:14.016
Was it half a carat?

07:14.600 --> 07:15.476
It was expensive.

07:16.394 --> 07:17.437
Flower-shaped.

07:17.520 --> 07:19.689
Yes, flower-shaped. Seriously!

07:19.772 --> 07:21.524
What would you even know?

07:21.607 --> 07:24.026
Oh dear, here it is.

07:24.569 --> 07:25.945
It's right over

07:26.946 --> 07:28.030
here.

07:29.782 --> 07:32.368
It just naturally rolled here on its own.

07:36.372 --> 07:39.125
You should call the police, shouldn't you?

07:39.208 --> 07:40.501
Lady, what are you doing?

07:40.585 --> 07:43.463
Call the police
and let them know you found the ring.

07:44.172 --> 07:45.548
Apologize for the mix-up.

07:45.631 --> 07:47.633
I'm asking you what you're doing.

07:49.510 --> 07:50.761
You won't call them?

07:53.973 --> 07:54.891
Lady!

07:59.812 --> 08:01.689
If you don't, I'll throw it away.

08:03.357 --> 08:04.650
You're out of your mind!

08:04.734 --> 08:06.986
Do you have any idea
how expensive that was?

08:07.069 --> 08:10.072
-Come on! Seriously!
-You've lost it anyway, right?

08:10.156 --> 08:13.284
You said it was stolen
and that the girl was the thief.

08:13.367 --> 08:16.412
And now you're going to report
that I've thrown it away?

08:17.497 --> 08:18.539
Damn it!

08:18.623 --> 08:19.540
Put it down!

08:19.624 --> 08:22.418
Don't you know me? I would throw this.

08:23.377 --> 08:24.837
Very far, in fact.

08:24.921 --> 08:26.255
-I'll--
-Hey!

08:29.425 --> 08:31.594
That ring is worth more than you are!

08:32.345 --> 08:33.179
Call them.

08:34.180 --> 08:37.433
Stay out of my fucking business.

08:38.017 --> 08:39.477
Apologize.

08:39.560 --> 08:41.646
Who do you think you are? Stay out of it!

08:41.729 --> 08:42.855
Do you know her?

08:43.481 --> 08:46.943
-I do.
-Seriously! You're driving me insane.

08:47.026 --> 08:48.819
Call them now!

09:00.581 --> 09:01.457
Hello?

09:02.875 --> 09:05.878
What now? Asking for money again?
We don't have any.

09:08.297 --> 09:09.549
Hey, Geum-myeong's mom!

09:10.049 --> 09:11.676
-Your daughter called!
-Okay.

09:12.343 --> 09:14.512
My baby! Oh my!

09:14.595 --> 09:15.680
"Baby"? Seriously?

09:16.806 --> 09:20.518
-Baby! Where are you?
-Baby's somewhere spending money!

09:21.686 --> 09:24.063
I wanted to cry like a baby

09:24.146 --> 09:26.440
and tell her that people in Seoul
were really evil.

09:26.524 --> 09:28.192
Baby, have you eaten?

09:28.985 --> 09:33.072
But that single sentence full of worries
left me speechless.

09:33.155 --> 09:34.907
Who hasn't eaten by now?

09:35.533 --> 09:36.784
My heart melted.

09:37.577 --> 09:39.704
No, I called just because.

09:41.205 --> 09:43.082
Can't I call just because I feel like it?

09:45.084 --> 09:46.127
I do.

09:48.546 --> 09:49.547
I have money.

09:52.466 --> 09:55.386
What about you? Is everything okay?

09:57.972 --> 10:01.601
Didn't I tell you to stop setting up
that stall on the street?

10:01.684 --> 10:05.479
I told you I hate
that you eat out on the street every day!

10:06.147 --> 10:09.025
Those damn abalones! Seriously!

10:09.108 --> 10:12.612
Is abalone season that important?
You always say your back hurts.

10:12.695 --> 10:15.531
Just open a store or something!

10:15.615 --> 10:18.159
You need money to open a store.

10:18.993 --> 10:19.827
Mom.

10:22.705 --> 10:24.749
Why don't you ever have any money?

10:27.877 --> 10:29.128
I know, right?

10:29.211 --> 10:31.631
Why don't I ever have any money?

10:31.714 --> 10:33.924
Because of you!

10:35.217 --> 10:37.303
I was mad at my mom for being poor.

10:38.179 --> 10:40.723
I was mad because I knew I was the reason.

10:42.767 --> 10:45.186
Baby, Dad hasn't arrived yet, has he?

10:45.269 --> 10:47.396
You didn't call
because you met him, did you?

10:47.480 --> 10:48.314
Dad?

10:48.397 --> 10:51.233
Dad received a reward
for saving that person from drowning.

10:51.317 --> 10:53.444
I told you it was happening today.

10:53.527 --> 10:58.658
The governor sent a group of co-op members
to the mainland to go sightseeing.

10:58.741 --> 11:03.371
He gave them museum tickets
because a new one opened.

11:03.454 --> 11:05.122
Where on the mainland? Which museum?

11:05.206 --> 11:08.084
He wants to see you
if he can find the time.

11:08.167 --> 11:09.377
Where on the mainland?

11:09.960 --> 11:14.131
On the mainland.
You know, the museum that just opened.

11:14.215 --> 11:17.760
You always just say "the mainland."
How am I supposed to know where that is?

11:17.843 --> 11:20.721
Which museum is he coming to?

11:20.805 --> 11:23.307
He'll visit if he can find the time?
I'm busy too!

11:23.391 --> 11:27.061
So is Dad coming or not?

11:27.728 --> 11:28.729
Geum-myeong.

11:28.813 --> 11:30.356
He'll be there.

11:30.856 --> 11:32.400
Dad will be there.

11:38.155 --> 11:39.699
-Kim Young-sam!
-Kim Dae-jung!

11:44.620 --> 11:46.747
Gosh, the traffic is awful.

11:47.998 --> 11:49.750
She's actually insane.

11:50.376 --> 11:52.002
How can she accuse you of stealing?

11:53.421 --> 11:55.047
So the cops called your house?

11:55.631 --> 11:56.465
No.

11:57.758 --> 11:59.802
I refused to give them
my home phone number.

12:05.224 --> 12:07.810
-You're not gonna tell your family?
-How could I?

12:12.314 --> 12:17.153
It's okay if the whole world knows,
as long as my mom and dad don't.

12:21.115 --> 12:22.324
Parents have no idea

12:23.534 --> 12:26.704
of the moment
when their child's heart develops knots.

12:28.956 --> 12:31.208
If they knew, they'd protect their child.

12:35.463 --> 12:37.089
So God keeps it from them.

12:42.094 --> 12:45.306
No tree grows without knots,

12:46.515 --> 12:50.311
and a child's knots would carve a hole
in a father's heart,

12:51.061 --> 12:52.688
so God keeps it hidden.

12:58.944 --> 12:59.862
Goodness me.

12:59.945 --> 13:03.073
You'll be the death of me.

13:03.574 --> 13:05.242
I could've been really late!

13:05.326 --> 13:07.578
It's cold. It gets colder at night.

13:08.162 --> 13:10.122
How long have you been waiting for me?

13:10.206 --> 13:12.166
All college students seem to cradle these.

13:12.249 --> 13:14.168
What time did you get here?

13:16.629 --> 13:18.130
Let's go. Come on.

13:20.257 --> 13:23.594
Doesn't this bother you?
Why is your bag strap always twisted?

13:52.248 --> 13:54.667
Did you come to Seoul to eat jjamppong?

13:55.209 --> 13:56.585
Aren't we going to talk?

13:59.213 --> 14:00.089
You drink too.

14:01.841 --> 14:03.050
I can hold my booze.

14:10.391 --> 14:12.977
Well, you're not into protests, are you?

14:13.060 --> 14:15.229
What museum opened?

14:15.855 --> 14:17.106
Where are you staying?

14:17.189 --> 14:18.566
I just stopped by.

14:19.149 --> 14:22.069
Tear gas is so painful.
The tears just won't stop.

14:22.152 --> 14:25.531
Which subway line is it?
Can you get there by yourself?

14:25.614 --> 14:26.657
Well,

14:27.783 --> 14:29.994
you're not dating a soldier, are you?

14:30.494 --> 14:31.912
You shouldn't date one.

14:32.621 --> 14:36.917
Why even eat together if it's like this?
Let's just each talk on our own.

14:45.843 --> 14:47.261
I quit my part-time job.

14:48.512 --> 14:50.306
I was asked to leave the dorms.

14:51.307 --> 14:52.933
I didn't get a scholarship.

14:56.812 --> 14:57.855
It's all good.

15:02.902 --> 15:05.321
This college is full of kids
who aced the state exam.

15:05.404 --> 15:08.782
Basically, all the dragons from streams
have gathered in one puddle.

15:09.283 --> 15:11.869
You can't always be the best.
No one's that perfect.

15:12.578 --> 15:16.123
I wouldn't even share a lunch table
with those kinds of kids.

15:21.879 --> 15:23.547
"A dragon from the stream."

15:24.882 --> 15:26.675
Why do I dislike hearing that?

15:30.137 --> 15:33.307
Who benefits if a dragon rises
from the stream?

15:34.642 --> 15:36.226
Is it any good for the stream?

15:37.937 --> 15:40.064
And what good is it for the dragon?

15:43.525 --> 15:45.277
I was selected to study abroad.

15:47.488 --> 15:48.614
But I'm not going to go.

15:51.825 --> 15:56.538
I really hate
that Oh Ye-rim is taking my place.

15:58.749 --> 15:59.917
But I just won't go.

16:07.925 --> 16:09.802
I want to study abroad too.

16:10.427 --> 16:12.304
I don't want that damn part-time job.

16:12.388 --> 16:14.556
I want to try everything.

16:16.642 --> 16:17.893
But I'm not going to.

16:20.896 --> 16:22.898
I'm just being greedy.

16:25.025 --> 16:26.902
It's just me being selfish.

16:31.031 --> 16:33.033
I want to soar higher and higher.

16:37.204 --> 16:39.206
But something keeps holding me back.

16:40.749 --> 16:42.084
Mom and I?

16:42.918 --> 16:43.752
No.

16:46.005 --> 16:46.964
Guilt.

16:48.841 --> 16:50.592
The higher I want to soar…

16:53.679 --> 16:55.806
the more guilt holds me back.

16:56.890 --> 17:00.227
Why should I feel bad
for wanting to do something more?

17:03.897 --> 17:05.774
It's so infuriating. I can't take it.

17:07.776 --> 17:10.446
All I ever wanted was to say I'm sorry,

17:11.030 --> 17:15.034
but when those tender words left my lips,
they always turned into barbs.

17:18.829 --> 17:19.663
Geum-myeong.

17:20.998 --> 17:21.832
What?

17:23.625 --> 17:24.460
Do it.

17:25.878 --> 17:26.795
Do it all.

17:29.131 --> 17:30.966
I'm still here for you.

17:44.104 --> 17:44.938
Geum-myeong,

17:45.564 --> 17:46.940
tell your teacher

17:47.483 --> 17:51.195
Dad will pay the school support fees
in three days.

17:56.825 --> 17:58.452
I'm still here for you.

18:06.001 --> 18:06.835
Am I a child?

18:06.919 --> 18:09.797
Why do you keep picking out the squid
and giving it to me?

18:12.341 --> 18:15.219
For the first time in 16 years,
citizens voted in the election,

18:15.302 --> 18:17.137
with 89.2% turnout…

18:17.221 --> 18:19.014
Find a safe place to stay.

18:19.098 --> 18:22.392
No need to worry about the rent at all.

18:23.060 --> 18:24.061
As for the money…

18:24.853 --> 18:28.357
The waters are full of fish.
I can catch them all.

18:30.984 --> 18:34.196
Don't date a soldier.
Don't drink hard liquor.

18:35.572 --> 18:36.990
Don't go to protests.

18:37.074 --> 18:39.868
Tear gas is extremely painful.
You can't stop crying.

18:41.328 --> 18:43.413
Reunification Democratic Party's
Kim Young-sam

18:43.497 --> 18:45.833
voted with his wife, Son Myung-soon.

18:46.542 --> 18:48.460
The news is what scares me the most.

18:48.961 --> 18:50.295
To be honest,

18:51.296 --> 18:52.214
I know nothing.

18:53.257 --> 18:54.383
I don't know anything.

18:54.466 --> 18:58.720
But I can't sleep when I see
soldiers with batons on the news.

18:58.804 --> 19:02.015
Just hearing about college kids
getting taken somewhere and beaten…

19:03.642 --> 19:04.852
Oh man.

19:07.521 --> 19:09.439
It sends shivers down my spine.

19:11.400 --> 19:12.693
So, Geum-myeong,

19:13.694 --> 19:14.820
if you can help it…

19:17.573 --> 19:20.576
Democratic Justice candidate Roh Tae-woo
is in the lead.

19:20.659 --> 19:24.454
Under the slogan
"A great era of ordinary people…"

19:25.038 --> 19:26.331
It's so annoying.

19:27.374 --> 19:28.208
What's wrong?

19:28.792 --> 19:31.044
Did you vote for someone else?

19:31.795 --> 19:33.714
You're annoying.

19:36.049 --> 19:38.093
You're so annoying, Dad.

19:42.306 --> 19:44.933
You call this just stopping by?

19:45.017 --> 19:47.561
You think the whole mainland
is just one place?

19:54.193 --> 19:56.612
Democratic Justice Party's Roh Tae-woo…

19:56.695 --> 19:58.030
You can't come home often.

19:59.114 --> 20:00.240
We're so far apart.

20:02.075 --> 20:04.703
Which museum is he coming to?

20:04.786 --> 20:07.539
He'll visit if he can find the time?
I'm busy too!

20:07.623 --> 20:10.876
So is Dad coming or not?

20:11.543 --> 20:16.173
Geum-myeong, he'll be there.
Dad will be there.

20:16.924 --> 20:20.719
When have you ever seen Dad
go sightseeing?

20:21.220 --> 20:24.973
Even on New Year's or Korean Thanksgiving,
he's eager to take his boat out to sea.

20:25.057 --> 20:26.642
He just used this chance

20:27.226 --> 20:28.852
as an excuse to see you.

20:29.937 --> 20:33.273
But I've got my own things
to do, too, you know?

20:33.857 --> 20:37.903
Dad went
because he really missed his eldest.

20:38.862 --> 20:41.365
So Geum-myeong, when you see your dad…

20:41.448 --> 20:44.117
YONGSAN INTERCITY BUS STATION

21:05.931 --> 21:08.392
Why would he come all the way
from Cheonan to Seoul?

21:09.893 --> 21:10.769
So annoying.

21:12.521 --> 21:13.480
So, Geum-myeong,

21:14.231 --> 21:17.234
when you see your dad,
don't get annoyed with him.

21:17.317 --> 21:19.236
Be sweet to your father, okay?

21:19.319 --> 21:21.613
His love has been one-sided for 20 years.

21:40.674 --> 21:42.301
Catch a lot of fish!

21:42.384 --> 21:44.469
Catch a lot of squids!

22:13.498 --> 22:16.418
Goodness me,
I'm leaving that little thing behind.

22:18.587 --> 22:22.424
Because of his daughter who,
in his eyes, refused to grow up,

22:22.924 --> 22:24.926
Dad thought he might again feel sorry…

22:27.929 --> 22:30.974
for his forever little girl, Ae-sun.

22:33.685 --> 22:36.146
FROM YANG EUN-MYEONG (CLASS 2-7)

22:36.730 --> 22:38.231
How can I put this?

22:38.899 --> 22:41.651
I'm not good at things like this!

22:43.695 --> 22:46.656
Tell the kids who bought the "S" letters
from you to return them.

22:46.740 --> 22:49.409
Just give them the money
and take them back!

22:49.493 --> 22:51.703
They keep saying
they don't have them anymore!

22:51.787 --> 22:53.580
Do you know how much this scotch costs?

22:53.663 --> 22:55.791
Do you know how long it takes
to earn this?

22:57.876 --> 22:58.919
Their fall was…

22:59.002 --> 23:00.837
Harvesting season, my foot.

23:00.921 --> 23:04.007
…not a season of harvest
but of being picked clean.

23:04.091 --> 23:07.677
You pick at me more and more as you age.
My fruit has been picked clean!

23:12.391 --> 23:15.727
HR teacher, Sonata. Principal, Stellar.
Chinese teacher, Pony, right?

23:15.811 --> 23:16.770
-Right?
-Yeah.

23:18.063 --> 23:19.564
Oh, teacher.

23:19.648 --> 23:21.108
Oh, hi.

23:22.567 --> 23:23.985
Hello, sir.

23:25.529 --> 23:26.363
Hello.

23:26.446 --> 23:29.199
It was fall when each was picked clean
of what had been sown.

23:35.664 --> 23:37.082
Is that your booze?

23:38.125 --> 23:40.836
Is that girl your daughter or a relative?

23:41.420 --> 23:43.171
What do you even know?

23:45.340 --> 23:46.466
I know her.

23:46.550 --> 23:48.051
Yes, I'm sure you do.

23:50.262 --> 23:52.431
-I don't need any more free stuff.
-That free stuff--

23:52.514 --> 23:54.891
If you get drunk, they'll rob you.

23:54.975 --> 23:56.935
She said you'll melt like butter, right?

23:57.686 --> 23:58.687
What are you saying?

23:58.770 --> 24:01.064
Don't turn the lights off, no matter what.

24:01.148 --> 24:02.983
That woman is a real thief.

24:03.066 --> 24:04.985
If you fall asleep, she'll steal your bag.

24:06.653 --> 24:07.988
Why tell me this?

24:09.114 --> 24:10.740
-Sorry?
-Why are you telling me?

24:20.959 --> 24:22.294
Why did you help me?

24:23.211 --> 24:24.379
Why did you even bother?

24:25.297 --> 24:26.256
Do you know me?

24:26.965 --> 24:28.008
What am I to you?

24:29.593 --> 24:30.427
Why?

24:31.386 --> 24:32.262
Why?

24:34.473 --> 24:35.515
It'd be upsetting.

24:36.475 --> 24:38.894
It'd be upsetting
if your bag got stolen too.

24:41.188 --> 24:42.022
Is that all?

24:43.440 --> 24:45.567
It's better if none of us are upset.

24:53.158 --> 24:54.075
You're right.

24:55.243 --> 24:57.496
It's better if none of us are upset.

25:09.007 --> 25:11.343
It's better if none of us are upset.

25:11.426 --> 25:14.596
It'd be upsetting
if the girl got wrongly accused of theft.

25:14.679 --> 25:17.807
You might as well be Mother Teresa.

25:18.558 --> 25:20.310
You don't know that girl.

25:20.393 --> 25:21.645
Do you even know SNU?

25:23.355 --> 25:25.815
You've always been so nosy.

25:27.526 --> 25:28.443
I do know her.

25:28.944 --> 25:31.655
She protected my mom's inheritance
when I was young.

25:31.738 --> 25:34.282
That girl wasn't even born then!

25:35.033 --> 25:37.827
-She's the spitting image of that girl.
-My goodness.

25:37.911 --> 25:40.622
If you weren't my old bar boss,
I'd have already…

25:40.705 --> 25:41.540
What?

25:42.374 --> 25:44.459
You'd make me a thief and fire me too?

25:48.964 --> 25:49.798
Miss Kim.

25:50.465 --> 25:51.299
Ma'am.

25:54.886 --> 25:55.720
Miss Kim.

25:55.804 --> 25:58.431
Stop calling me "Miss Kim"
in front of my daughter.

25:58.932 --> 26:02.227
Why live such a shameful life
if you're scared of your kid's judgment?

26:03.061 --> 26:05.772
Your daughter is watching everything.

26:06.773 --> 26:09.651
Damn it! I told you to throw away
the empty ones!

26:10.360 --> 26:13.655
Live a life of virtue, I'm telling you.

26:13.738 --> 26:15.574
The parents' virtues and karma

26:16.074 --> 26:17.909
go straight to the child.

26:18.827 --> 26:19.661
Look at her.

26:20.662 --> 26:21.496
You can tell

26:22.330 --> 26:23.915
she's already on the wrong path.

26:24.666 --> 26:26.084
I know.

26:38.471 --> 26:39.764
My mom made me do it.

26:41.850 --> 26:45.395
SEOUL STATION

26:57.741 --> 26:59.784
How can I leave when you look like this?

26:59.868 --> 27:02.287
Then don't leave!

27:05.498 --> 27:07.584
Are we back together, then?

27:08.418 --> 27:11.588
I don't know. Just stay still for now.

27:11.671 --> 27:14.841
Stop breaking my heart.
I might end up becoming a deserter.

27:16.259 --> 27:17.594
How many days are left?

27:18.887 --> 27:19.929
797 days.

27:23.266 --> 27:26.353
I hate North Korea so much!

27:26.436 --> 27:29.564
I can't do much
about our on-and-off relationship.

27:29.648 --> 27:31.733
But just marry me in the end, okay?

27:32.567 --> 27:33.568
It depends.

27:34.444 --> 27:35.445
On how well you do.

27:35.528 --> 27:37.155
You said you'd marry me last time.

27:37.238 --> 27:40.241
Hey, who knows what will happen?

27:40.742 --> 27:43.912
They say you don't know
until you walk down the aisle.

27:45.163 --> 27:46.331
Just wait and see.

27:46.956 --> 27:48.708
I'll see you in a wedding dress.

27:49.209 --> 27:51.169
I truly believed I was different from Mom.

27:51.252 --> 27:53.213
Hey, are you getting on or what?

27:54.089 --> 27:56.800
In the end,
it was like mother, like daughter,

27:57.967 --> 27:59.260
though not entirely.

28:03.640 --> 28:06.059
The bride will now enter
and walk down the aisle.

28:08.436 --> 28:09.312
Geum-myeong.

28:11.022 --> 28:12.732
Dad's still right here.

28:13.525 --> 28:15.819
Just do everything you want to do.

28:31.501 --> 28:33.461
Mom's love was a fairy tale.

28:33.545 --> 28:35.505
Please welcome the bride.

28:40.427 --> 28:43.972
Will my story also be a fairy tale?

28:45.265 --> 28:46.933
'67 THE 7TH HALLA CHUNSA FESTIVAL

28:57.318 --> 29:00.238
Ice pops!

29:00.739 --> 29:02.240
-Here, enjoy.
-Thank you.

29:02.323 --> 29:03.825
Ice pops!

29:10.248 --> 29:12.041
THEME
JEJU, SPRING BREEZE, WIND

29:28.475 --> 29:29.559
"Jeju."

29:29.642 --> 29:32.353
"By Oh Ae-sun
from Dodong Girls' High, class 1-5."

29:34.272 --> 29:35.607
Ten million waves

29:36.107 --> 29:37.650
Ten million winds

29:38.151 --> 29:39.486
Yet a rock still stands

29:40.403 --> 29:44.240
A rock that never erodes
In the sea of my heart

29:58.129 --> 29:58.963
Mom.

30:07.180 --> 30:09.557
I told you not to sit next to me.

30:09.641 --> 30:11.434
Go back to your side!

30:12.769 --> 30:16.064
What's an athlete doing
in the writing contest? Who sent you here?

30:16.689 --> 30:19.567
I raised my hand
and said I wanted to enter.

30:20.860 --> 30:22.946
You know what they say around town?

30:23.029 --> 30:26.908
They say Gwan-sik wakes up
just to follow Ae-sun around.

30:26.991 --> 30:29.327
I think you'll be the winner this time.

30:31.246 --> 30:33.540
I think you'll be a great poet.

30:34.165 --> 30:35.208
A great poet.

30:37.585 --> 30:39.128
-Really?
-Yes.

30:40.880 --> 30:42.173
What would you know?

30:43.424 --> 30:44.342
I don't.

30:45.343 --> 30:46.177
I can't write.

30:58.439 --> 31:00.191
I should write to the Ministry.

31:00.775 --> 31:02.694
They need to make athletes study too.

31:02.777 --> 31:04.612
Will they take responsibility
for this kid's life?

31:04.696 --> 31:05.697
SPRING BREEZE

31:05.780 --> 31:07.240
I'm so upset, seriously.

31:07.323 --> 31:08.908
THE WIND GOES WHOOSH
MY HEART GOES BOO-HOO

31:09.659 --> 31:11.578
Erase the moth. Why did you draw it here?

31:11.661 --> 31:13.204
It's a butterfly.

31:14.497 --> 31:15.874
Write a poem for me too.

31:17.166 --> 31:19.127
Titled "Yang Gwan-sik."

31:21.754 --> 31:22.589
Why would I?

31:44.652 --> 31:48.197
In life, you never know what will happen
unless you go for it.

31:48.948 --> 31:53.828
Who knew I'd still be sitting here
20 years later?

31:53.912 --> 31:57.582
THE 28TH HALLA CHUNSA WRITING CONTEST

31:57.665 --> 31:59.792
THEME
SPRING, WIND, MOON

32:01.002 --> 32:01.836
Submit this.

32:02.921 --> 32:04.631
FALL BREEZE
OH AE-SUN

32:04.714 --> 32:06.299
I'm not in high school anymore.

32:07.508 --> 32:11.137
The paper was lying on the ground,
so I scribbled a few lines.

32:11.679 --> 32:13.556
I still think you should submit it.

32:14.390 --> 32:15.642
Submit what? Forget it.

32:16.893 --> 32:19.896
Tomorrow's sports day is canceled too.

32:19.979 --> 32:20.855
Why?

32:20.939 --> 32:24.067
They're rehearsing for the Olympics too.

32:26.819 --> 32:28.655
We earn the most on sports days.

32:29.697 --> 32:32.951
We should set up our own place,
even if it means going into debt.

32:33.034 --> 32:36.746
I'm sick and tired of
this bundle-carrying life.

32:38.581 --> 32:39.415
Excuse me.

32:39.916 --> 32:42.710
Hello. Would you like some mini snails?

32:42.794 --> 32:45.254
Ae-sun? You're Oh Ae-sun, right?

32:45.338 --> 32:47.298
It's Chang-suk. Go Chang-suk.

32:47.382 --> 32:48.967
We went to high school together.

32:50.551 --> 32:53.388
Oh, Chang-suk.

32:53.972 --> 32:57.183
It's been ages.
I haven't seen you since you left school.

32:57.767 --> 33:01.604
The others are wondering how you're doing.
You don't even attend school reunions.

33:02.105 --> 33:03.690
Don't you get those?

33:03.773 --> 33:05.191
The reunion postcards?

33:05.274 --> 33:08.027
Maybe you're not on the list
because you dropped out?

33:09.362 --> 33:11.906
I'll just give this to you for free.

33:11.990 --> 33:14.158
I'll give you plenty.

33:14.867 --> 33:17.745
Gosh, she can't even look.

33:19.080 --> 33:21.499
Why? Is she embarrassed
about getting expelled?

33:21.582 --> 33:24.544
No, not her high school friend.

33:34.262 --> 33:37.306
Mom could never bear
to look at kids that age.

33:42.145 --> 33:43.771
Hey, it's not here.

33:44.939 --> 33:45.898
How old are you?

33:46.858 --> 33:47.734
Fifteen.

33:48.317 --> 33:50.820
Fifteen, born in the Year of the Tiger.

33:51.779 --> 33:52.613
Yes.

33:55.908 --> 33:56.784
Here it is.

33:56.868 --> 33:57.994
Hey, where?

33:59.829 --> 34:01.372
Is that popular these days?

34:02.415 --> 34:04.709
-Sorry?
-What else is popular?

34:05.460 --> 34:07.545
-Thank you.
-Thank you so much.

34:08.254 --> 34:10.465
Sure, enjoy them all.

34:10.548 --> 34:11.382
Yes, sir.

34:15.636 --> 34:20.600
In Dad's heart,
Dong-myeong was still growing up.

34:23.603 --> 34:26.522
I believe sympathy is part of evolution.

34:27.273 --> 34:31.069
Look at the old women in the countryside.
They're fine after losing their kids.

34:31.152 --> 34:33.488
They'd say,
"I had eight kids and two died."

34:33.571 --> 34:37.158
"You had a brother once,"
as if it were nothing.

34:37.742 --> 34:40.161
How can they?
How do you go on after losing a child?

34:40.828 --> 34:42.205
But they carry on just fine.

34:42.288 --> 34:45.249
What are they supposed to do?
Cry every day? Starve?

34:45.833 --> 34:47.376
No, the point of our presentation

34:47.460 --> 34:50.880
is to prove the correlation
between sympathy and civilization.

34:51.547 --> 34:52.381
Right?

34:55.176 --> 34:56.177
Are they below you?

34:59.263 --> 35:00.098
What?

35:00.681 --> 35:03.434
You think they are like that
because they're lesser than you?

35:06.062 --> 35:08.106
Just keep playing with your eraser.

35:09.357 --> 35:12.068
It's not because
they're not as admirable as you.

35:12.151 --> 35:15.321
They don't act like nothing's wrong
because they're less evolved.

35:15.905 --> 35:17.782
They move on because they have to.

35:20.076 --> 35:23.037
Geum-myeong, I'm sorry to say this.

35:24.705 --> 35:25.998
Do you feel inferior to me?

35:27.583 --> 35:28.417
Why would I be?

35:29.168 --> 35:33.089
Well, for several reasons.
You even lost your chance to study abroad.

35:33.172 --> 35:36.008
Did I lose it? I'm just letting you go.

35:36.092 --> 35:37.135
Letting me go?

35:41.848 --> 35:42.974
Then you should go.

35:44.350 --> 35:45.351
You can go.

35:55.778 --> 35:57.738
You keep acting like you're letting me go,

35:57.822 --> 36:01.117
but you don't get to go
just because your GPA is higher.

36:01.200 --> 36:03.119
Family background
and circumstances count too.

36:03.703 --> 36:04.537
Who said that?

36:05.538 --> 36:06.372
Your father again?

36:07.832 --> 36:09.709
Life's about the total score in the end.

36:16.799 --> 36:19.051
I'm the one who got 37 votes.

36:19.135 --> 36:20.761
So what if you got 37 votes?

36:20.845 --> 36:22.555
Do your 37 votes matter now?

36:22.638 --> 36:26.058
In real life,
37 votes don't mean anything!

36:26.142 --> 36:27.977
Between you and Man-ki,

36:28.936 --> 36:32.648
there's something that goes
beyond just nine votes, okay?

36:36.027 --> 36:36.861
Take it.

36:37.737 --> 36:39.113
Yeah, here. Take it.

36:40.364 --> 36:42.200
Leave it here. Take one.

36:43.659 --> 36:46.537
Man-ki's dad brought these
to celebrate him becoming president.

36:47.038 --> 36:48.831
He treated you last time, right?

36:48.915 --> 36:52.877
You should feel guilty
if you took a bun and didn't vote for him.

37:09.894 --> 37:13.689
If you have to stay behind,
you'll get one only after you're done.

37:18.444 --> 37:19.362
Yeah, take one.

37:20.988 --> 37:22.031
Take one.

37:28.829 --> 37:30.081
DIARY
OH AE-SUN

37:49.892 --> 37:52.478
Man-ki! Are you even studying properly?

37:53.062 --> 37:55.690
You're not just eating cream buns
at home, are you?

37:55.773 --> 37:57.817
Our class president is a fake president.

37:57.900 --> 37:59.277
He's a cream bun president.

37:59.360 --> 38:03.281
Even if he has 100 cream buns,
Lee Man-ki will never get 100 points.

38:03.364 --> 38:05.032
But I got 100 points.

38:16.460 --> 38:19.630
Mom was like a wildflower
that finds its way to the sunlight,

38:19.714 --> 38:22.675
even if it was under a dark brick wall.

38:22.758 --> 38:23.884
Let's hurry.

38:23.968 --> 38:26.971
In the end,
she would always find the light.

38:27.054 --> 38:28.180
Careful.

38:29.348 --> 38:33.102
This is where I was set up on a date
with Bu Sang-gil back in the day.

38:35.021 --> 38:39.525
At the time,
I really thought my life was over.

38:43.654 --> 38:46.991
I heard you really wanted
a man from Seoul.

38:48.242 --> 38:51.329
I'm pretty much from Seoul.

38:52.288 --> 38:53.706
Right after Korea's liberation,

38:53.789 --> 38:56.375
my wealthy family sent me
to study in Seoul.

38:57.543 --> 38:59.920
If I hadn't married and moved down here,

39:00.713 --> 39:02.465
I could've been a man of power.

39:06.802 --> 39:09.096
At the beginning of my first marriage…

39:10.473 --> 39:12.433
Am I getting that tea anytime today?

39:19.190 --> 39:21.150
Don't worry about what I think.

39:22.360 --> 39:23.194
Love isn't…

39:23.277 --> 39:24.278
Goodness.

39:25.738 --> 39:28.157
Who would've thought I'd own this place?

39:28.824 --> 39:32.536
As I said, in life, you never know
what will happen unless you go for it.

39:32.620 --> 39:34.372
Go!

39:34.455 --> 39:38.042
I even thought of the name of this place.

39:39.460 --> 39:40.461
That's right.

39:40.544 --> 39:43.255
The shop name should be chosen
by someone well-educated.

39:43.881 --> 39:46.967
"Sun and the Three Aunties'."

39:47.676 --> 39:49.845
Why bother with a complicated name?

39:49.929 --> 39:52.890
Even poetry collections sell better
with a simple title.

39:52.973 --> 39:55.810
This land has thousands of people
with "Sun" in their names,

39:55.893 --> 39:58.020
so attracting them would be enough, right?

39:58.104 --> 39:59.188
Yeah, that's right.

39:59.271 --> 40:01.816
-Your name gets top billing.
-Let her do it.

40:03.984 --> 40:07.113
Let's stop having lunch on the street.

40:07.696 --> 40:10.825
From now on,
I'm only eating at the dining table.

40:11.450 --> 40:12.827
You eat at the table.

40:12.910 --> 40:14.870
So each of us gets a quarter, okay?

40:14.954 --> 40:18.833
Ae-sun, you just pay this much.
We'll cover the rest.

40:19.333 --> 40:20.626
The water pressure is low.

40:20.709 --> 40:21.544
What?

40:22.044 --> 40:23.462
The water pressure…

40:23.546 --> 40:27.925
This is enough. You can wash
sea cucumbers and sea squirts with it.

40:28.551 --> 40:29.468
I'll wash them all.

40:29.552 --> 40:35.099
However, while the faucet barely dripped,
steady and diligent,

40:36.767 --> 40:39.562
the leaking hole was gushing relentlessly.

40:41.147 --> 40:43.107
ELIGIBILITY FOR STATE-FUNDED STUDY ABROAD

40:43.190 --> 40:47.903
I just find it funny
that an English major is going to Japan.

40:48.654 --> 40:52.366
It also means I'll graduate later,
so I probably shouldn't…

40:54.118 --> 40:55.744
I don't think I should…

41:04.587 --> 41:07.715
I… want you to go.

41:09.925 --> 41:11.469
Ye-rim is a bit…

41:13.554 --> 41:14.430
snobbish.

41:20.895 --> 41:24.273
Since you don't qualify
for the state-funded scholarship,

41:25.649 --> 41:27.318
as I mentioned before…

41:27.401 --> 41:29.528
Oh no, please don't do that.

41:29.612 --> 41:33.324
I'm going to leave.
I won't come back if you call me again.

41:33.407 --> 41:36.285
Come on. I'm quite well off, you know?

41:37.578 --> 41:38.996
You can pay me back later.

41:40.623 --> 41:43.584
You said your car was the cheapest
in the faculty parking lot.

41:44.168 --> 41:47.546
It's not the time to be worrying about me.
Be brazen at times like this!

41:47.630 --> 41:49.256
Or you'll end up like me.

41:50.257 --> 41:52.718
But you're really amazing.

41:52.801 --> 41:56.847
I think you're the only professor
who gives apples to sparrows.

41:58.891 --> 42:02.645
I'm truly grateful
that you are looking out for me.

42:04.897 --> 42:06.774
I feel like I've already been to Japan.

42:07.650 --> 42:09.693
Even your words are pretty.

42:11.987 --> 42:15.658
When I spoke to others,
it was as if I were writing a love letter.

42:16.158 --> 42:19.036
I would choose my words carefully,
one by one.

42:20.287 --> 42:23.123
Yeah, she's such a great person.
A really great person.

42:23.624 --> 42:27.711
When others treat you well,
even just once, they become your savior.

42:28.879 --> 42:31.674
Yeah, so you have to send
the best tangerines you can find.

42:31.757 --> 42:33.634
She's so good to me.

42:34.134 --> 42:35.594
So what does she do for you?

42:35.678 --> 42:37.680
Does she say she likes you
or you're doing well?

42:38.180 --> 42:41.850
What did she say?
I want to hear it and feel happy too!

42:41.934 --> 42:45.688
She wants to lend me money
so I can study abroad.

42:46.272 --> 42:47.815
It's not easy to do for others.

42:48.315 --> 42:51.360
She takes only me to the faculty cafeteria
and buys me lunch.

42:51.986 --> 42:53.362
But you said

42:54.405 --> 42:56.907
you didn't really want to study abroad.

42:56.991 --> 43:00.035
Just send a box of tangerines.

43:00.536 --> 43:04.081
Do you want to study abroad?
You want to go?

43:04.164 --> 43:06.500
So what if I want to go?

43:07.668 --> 43:09.086
Can I even go?

43:09.169 --> 43:10.212
How much is it?

43:10.921 --> 43:12.214
Come on, how much is it?

43:13.382 --> 43:14.550
You don't need to know.

43:14.633 --> 43:18.053
I'm not saying I'll pay for it.
Just tell me approximately how much.

43:18.137 --> 43:19.555
Mom, don't you watch TV?

43:20.180 --> 43:21.432
The yen is crazy high now.

43:21.515 --> 43:24.268
But you could at least tell me
the approximate cost.

43:24.351 --> 43:26.145
You're really starting to make me mad.

43:26.228 --> 43:28.230
Are you a beggar? Don't you have parents?

43:28.314 --> 43:30.399
Why would others offer to lend you money?

43:30.482 --> 43:31.900
What on earth are you doing?

43:31.984 --> 43:34.153
You think I look like
I'm from a wealthy family?

43:34.236 --> 43:37.448
I'm not going to Japan,
so everyone knows we're not well-off.

43:37.531 --> 43:40.659
So how much is it?
Just tell me how much it is!

43:40.743 --> 43:43.746
And what if I tell you? You gonna send me
with money from the stall?

43:43.829 --> 43:45.706
If you have the money,
stop selling at the stall!

43:45.789 --> 43:48.167
Gosh, I want to stop too. I really do.

43:48.250 --> 43:49.209
But how can I?

43:54.381 --> 43:57.801
Whatever, just forget it.
Don't bother sending the tangerines.

43:58.302 --> 44:00.262
Talking to you is just so annoying.

44:01.722 --> 44:04.975
But I treated the savior
to whom I'm a million times grateful

44:05.059 --> 44:06.935
like scrap paper.

44:10.814 --> 44:12.066
What now?

44:13.400 --> 44:18.113
I wasn't careful
with my words or my feelings.

44:27.539 --> 44:29.291
I'm not eligible whatsoever.

45:23.762 --> 45:24.847
How much is it?

45:24.930 --> 45:28.434
Just 300 won. Give me 300 won.

45:43.615 --> 45:45.451
How much for all of it?

45:45.534 --> 45:46.368
Huh?

45:47.244 --> 45:48.495
I like beans.

45:49.872 --> 45:53.000
A kind-hearted mother
gave birth to a kind-hearted daughter.

45:53.083 --> 45:55.419
They would always adore each other

45:56.837 --> 45:58.630
and break each other's hearts.

46:04.428 --> 46:06.430
I want to stop selling on the street too.

46:06.930 --> 46:09.683
Who in the world
wants to make a living as a street vendor?

46:12.811 --> 46:14.313
I used to be coy as well.

46:14.938 --> 46:16.732
I used to get called Literary Girl.

46:18.358 --> 46:22.821
When I run into a high school friend
while eating on newspaper in the market,

46:23.322 --> 46:25.574
I just want to stop eating.

46:26.283 --> 46:27.993
I lose my appetite for the whole day.

46:35.876 --> 46:38.921
Is she the only one with pride?
Am I like this because I lack it?

46:40.881 --> 46:41.715
But what can I do?

46:41.799 --> 46:44.092
She has so many things she wants to do,

46:44.176 --> 46:46.887
and not being able to help
kills me inside.

46:53.018 --> 46:57.523
Strange how you started asking for liquor
after seeing your beloved daughter.

46:59.024 --> 46:59.858
You know,

47:01.276 --> 47:04.488
I have nothing to say to you or her.

47:09.827 --> 47:11.495
My mom must've cried her eyes out

47:13.038 --> 47:17.668
when I didn't become class president
due to mental and financial limitations.

47:19.586 --> 47:21.547
I only get it now.

47:28.762 --> 47:29.596
What did she say?

47:30.806 --> 47:34.351
Did she cry about wanting to study abroad?
She cried out of frustration, right?

47:36.728 --> 47:39.147
For the daughter who would never grow up,

47:39.731 --> 47:42.609
they ended up selling that house.

47:46.947 --> 47:49.449
These are the last persimmons, right?

47:50.784 --> 47:53.203
Eat them all. Don't give any away.

47:55.163 --> 47:56.373
Not even to our kids?

47:56.874 --> 47:59.334
Not even to our kids.
Only you can eat them.

48:01.420 --> 48:07.092
The more the kids grow,
the more they pick us clean, right?

48:07.175 --> 48:09.386
Didn't you know
this was a losing business?

48:11.889 --> 48:13.307
They left behind the house

48:15.142 --> 48:17.102
where Ae-sun's mother, little Ae-sun…

48:19.354 --> 48:21.440
and the one whose name they dared not say,

48:22.524 --> 48:25.944
Dong-myeong, would be missed.

49:50.237 --> 49:53.281
Mom, I didn't realize how young you were.

49:54.616 --> 49:57.411
You need to get rid of the chipped ones!

49:58.578 --> 50:02.541
You visited my dream when we moved here.
Are you back because we're leaving?

50:03.458 --> 50:05.377
You're so stingy.

50:06.128 --> 50:08.005
You should've visited my dreams more.

50:09.673 --> 50:11.341
Mom, I'm upset.

50:11.425 --> 50:14.928
I have so much I want to say to my mom.

50:16.638 --> 50:19.641
What's the point of writing that?
He can't even read.

50:21.393 --> 50:23.520
He didn't learn to read.
How can he read it?

50:24.730 --> 50:28.150
Just in case he comes over here
during the holidays

50:28.233 --> 50:30.193
and is surprised Mommy isn't here.

50:32.779 --> 50:34.489
I didn't want to scare the baby.

50:41.872 --> 50:44.833
Do you and Gwan-sik
still never talk about him?

50:48.295 --> 50:50.714
Don't you talk to him about Dong-myeong?

50:56.053 --> 50:57.012
Why would we?

50:58.805 --> 51:00.974
We already know how each other feels.

51:01.475 --> 51:05.812
Any other grief fades with time
and becomes numb.

51:06.396 --> 51:08.065
But when the grief is too deep,

51:08.690 --> 51:09.816
when it's too deep,

51:11.151 --> 51:12.277
I end up burying it.

51:13.487 --> 51:14.988
I just can't bring it up.

51:20.494 --> 51:21.328
Ae-sun.

51:23.371 --> 51:24.206
Talk to him.

51:25.457 --> 51:26.291
Pour it all out.

51:27.250 --> 51:28.418
Even the deep ocean

51:29.669 --> 51:30.504
uses the waves

51:31.797 --> 51:33.381
to pour out restlessly.

51:40.889 --> 51:42.307
I'm sorry to say this to you.

51:43.642 --> 51:48.105
I know it's not fair,
but I can bear to reminisce about you.

51:50.398 --> 51:51.691
Not my baby though.

51:53.068 --> 51:54.653
It's not possible with a child.

52:05.831 --> 52:08.041
All I wanted was
for you to have a good life.

52:09.876 --> 52:11.586
How will my baby go on?

52:12.796 --> 52:14.965
How has my baby survived the pain?

52:18.426 --> 52:22.597
I just forget briefly from time to time.

52:24.015 --> 52:25.308
Just from time to time.

52:29.271 --> 52:31.523
Somehow, life goes on.

52:58.341 --> 53:00.594
THE MOON WANES,

53:00.677 --> 53:03.597
YET THE YOUNG HEART REMAINS.

53:03.680 --> 53:04.806
Tomorrow…

53:04.890 --> 53:06.474
Hurry, this way.

53:09.060 --> 53:12.272
…life will go on
under the blazing sun of tomorrow.

53:12.355 --> 53:13.190
Careful.

53:17.068 --> 53:20.614
Damn those planes.
Why are there so many of them?

53:31.208 --> 53:32.459
Ladies and gentlemen,

53:32.542 --> 53:35.295
we are now arriving
at New Tokyo International Airport.

53:35.378 --> 53:38.089
-Hey, can you empty this ashtray?
-Yes, sir.

53:39.049 --> 53:40.800
Ladies and gentlemen,

53:40.884 --> 53:44.846
we are now arriving
at New Tokyo International Airport.

53:45.347 --> 53:49.142
The local time is 11:50 a.m.

53:53.480 --> 53:55.899
Why did she wrap it over and over?

53:57.400 --> 53:59.569
Why did she wrap it like this?

54:00.445 --> 54:01.404
Seriously.

54:34.354 --> 54:36.606
Have some, crybaby.

54:41.653 --> 54:43.196
Thank you.

54:43.280 --> 54:44.155
No problem.

55:00.880 --> 55:04.301
I swallowed their dreams
and spread my wings,

55:05.218 --> 55:08.847
embracing my mom's dream
like a seed in my heart.

55:25.447 --> 55:27.574
Is this funny? Is this funny to you?

55:29.576 --> 55:30.910
That damn studying…

55:33.163 --> 55:37.834
How I really wanted to do it so badly.

55:40.086 --> 55:44.507
But now my daughter
is even going to study abroad.

55:45.592 --> 55:47.552
It's so thrilling, isn't it?

55:47.635 --> 55:48.845
How fantastic is that?

55:48.928 --> 55:50.263
So are you happy?

55:57.270 --> 55:58.480
Mom!

55:59.481 --> 56:01.691
Mom!

56:02.692 --> 56:05.403
Mom's dream was passed on to me…

56:11.159 --> 56:14.537
Mom's dream was passed on to me…

56:21.169 --> 56:24.756
a dream so heavy, a dream so blazing…

56:26.424 --> 56:29.010
When you guys soar,

56:30.011 --> 56:33.014
I swear it feels like I'm soaring too.

56:34.099 --> 56:36.851
…that, at last,
it made the sound of wings flapping.

56:38.520 --> 56:41.856
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

56:45.276 --> 56:46.194
DODONG GIRLS' HIGH

56:51.533 --> 56:54.077
Did you get Ae-sun's permission?

56:55.203 --> 56:57.414
Why limit writing contests to kids?

56:57.497 --> 57:01.709
Sauces taste better when fermented.
One knows life better after living it.

57:02.293 --> 57:04.421
Kids don't know life's thorns and burdens.

57:04.921 --> 57:06.714
Once again,

57:06.798 --> 57:10.051
if there is a student named Oh Ae-sun,

57:10.135 --> 57:13.263
please come to the faculty office
immediately.

57:13.346 --> 57:14.264
Oh Ae-sun.

57:14.347 --> 57:16.141
When the students are taking tests,

57:16.224 --> 57:20.979
there are always some students
who never write their grade and class,

57:21.062 --> 57:23.273
no matter how many times you remind them.

57:24.107 --> 57:27.735
Did I or did I not tell you
that you must tell them countless times?

57:29.612 --> 57:30.822
Did I or did I not?

57:32.782 --> 57:34.159
Am I talking to a wall?

57:34.826 --> 57:37.704
The winner is from our school,
and we can't find the student.

57:37.787 --> 57:40.248
What am I supposed to tell the principal?

57:41.708 --> 57:43.376
Goodness gracious.

57:43.877 --> 57:46.713
EVEN AS I GENTLY PRESS MY HEART
TO SOOTHE IT DOWN

57:46.796 --> 57:49.382
THE MOON WANES,
YET THE YOUNG HEART REMAINS.

01:00:34.839 --> 01:00:39.802
"IN THE HOPE THAT OUR ECHOES
WILL FLOW AND FLOW UNTIL THEY REACH YOU."

01:00:46.934 --> 01:00:49.145
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
